/-!
# The presentation of the Suzuki sporadic group holds in its permutation model

The presentation selected for `Suz` (`TauCeti.Sporadic.suzPresentation`) has seven involutions
`a`, …, `g` as generators and thirty-four relators: the Coxeter relations of the two paths
`a5b3c8d3e` and `b3f4g3b`, and the six further relations `a = (cd)⁴`, `a = (fg)²`, `(abcf)⁵`,
`(bfg)⁵`, `((bcdcd)⁵e)³` and `(abcg)⁵`. The generators `Suz.a`, …, `Suz.f` of the degree-1782 model
`TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz` have orders `3` and `10`, so they are not such a family. This file gives
seven involutions `Suz.imageA`, …, `Suz.imageG` of the `1782` points that satisfy all thirty-four
relators and generate exactly the model `Suz`, and deduces that the presented group
`SporadicName.Suz.Group` maps onto the model. In particular the presented group is nontrivial.

Each image is given by its table of images, so that the relators compute directly. Each is also
written as a word in the generators of the model (`Suz.imageA_eq`, …, `Suz.imageG_eq`), which puts
it in the model; conversely `Suz.a_eq`, …, `Suz.f_eq` write the six generators of the model as
words in the seven images, so the images generate the whole model.

The seven permutations were found by computer: a coset enumeration of the presentation over the
subgroup generated by `a`, …, `f` closes with `1782` cosets, and the resulting action on the
cosets was carried to the point numbering of the model by an isomorphism between the two graphs
of valency `416` that the two actions preserve; the words come from a search in the Cayley graphs.
Nothing about that computation is used: the relators and both directions of generation are checked
here. Products follow Mathlib's convention `(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`, and it is in this convention that
the relators are evaluated.

No order of the model or of the presented group is asserted here, and the surjection is not shown
to be injective.

The lift and range arguments use `GroupPresentation.homEquiv` and
`GroupPresentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq`.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.imageA`, …, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.imageG`: the images of the seven
  generators, with `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.presentationImage` the resulting assignment.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: the thirty-four relators hold.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.presentationHom`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.range_presentationHom`: the
  homomorphism from the presented group and its range.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_Suz`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## References

* R. Lindenbergh, *Group Presentations Library*, version 1.0, record `GPLTable.Suz.1`,
  <https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g>, for the presentation.
* C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, *Low Rank Representations and Graphs for Sporadic Groups*,
  Cambridge University Press, 1997, Chapter 4, doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005.
* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Suz` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>, for the model in whose point numbering
  the images are given.
-/

